# =============================================================================
# .GITIGNORE — Job Application Pipeline
# RULE: if it contains personal data, credentials, or runtime state → exclude
#
# IMPORTANT: git does NOT support trailing "# comment" text on a pattern line
# — only a line that STARTS with # is a comment. A pattern like
# "*.enc   # encrypted files" is treated as one literal (and unmatchable)
# pattern, not as "*.enc" plus a comment. Every note below is on its own line
# for that reason — do not put explanatory text on the same line as a pattern.
# =============================================================================

# ── Credentials & secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API keys, email password, Workday password, secret key
.env
# encrypted credential stores
*.enc
# Workday account list with credentials (incl. archived plaintext backups)
workday_accounts*.json
# encryption key
secure_store.key

# ── Personal profile (contains real name, email, phone, address, experience) ──
# private — use raghav_profile.example.py as template
raghav_profile.py

# ── Personal Q&A and auto-saved Claude answers ────────────────────────────────
# contains personal answers (salary, address, work auth)
qa_answers.py
# auto-saved Claude answers — may contain personal data
claude_answers.py

# ── Application data & logs (personal job search history) ────────────────────
# Fixed 2026-09-13: found LIVE on the public repo — greenhouse_applied_log.json,
# receipts.json, submitted_applications.json, crash_logs/, indeed_handoff.html
# and several others were never covered by the specific patterns below and got
# committed with real personal data (name, LinkedIn, school, work-auth answers,
# 316+ application records). Broadened to a whole-directory ignore instead of
# maintaining a per-file list that a new log/cache file can silently slip past.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
# Exception, added 2026-09-13: this is a public, non-personal list of 8,317
# real Greenhouse company slugs (from github.com/Feashliaa/job-board-aggregator,
# MIT/CC BY-NC 4.0) that the expanded-discovery feature reads from. Without
# this exception, anyone who clones the repo gets a working pipeline but the
# expanded-discovery feature silently has nothing to read — shipping it is
# what makes GREENHOUSE_USE_EXPANDED_DISCOVERY actually usable out of the box.
!data/greenhouse_companies_full.json
# (previously listed here individually — now covered by the blanket rule above,
# kept as documentation of what's actually personal: apply_log.json,
# indeed_applied_log.json, workday_applied_log.json, linkedin_applied_log.json,
# apply_queue.json, Application_Tracker.xlsx, stuck_questions.json, *.db,
# answer_bank*.json/csv, desc_fingerprints.json, greenhouse_applied_log.json,
# receipts.json, submitted_applications.json, score_cache.json,
# stuck_submits.json, gh_skip_cache.json, ai_interviews_pending.json,
# crash_logs/, indeed_handoff.html, and any future runtime/log file added here.

# ── Runtime logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/*.log
data/runs/
pipeline_log.txt
pipeline_run_log.txt
*.log
*_error.log
*_error.md
phase4_errors.md
evening_pipeline_report_*.txt
evening_report_*.txt
afternoon_summary_*.txt
claude_task_*.log

# ── Browser session files (contain login cookies) ─────────────────────────────
# Exact per-platform session profiles.
.indeed_session/
.linkedin_session/
.workday_session/
.greenhouse_session/
# Any variant/backup/renamed copy of the above — e.g. the "corrupted_backup"
# and timestamped snapshots that don't match the exact names above. Added
# 2026-08-25 after .indeed_session_corrupted_backup_20260708_1615/ (318,402
# files — a full Chrome profile: Cookies, Login Data, History, Web Data,
# Trust Tokens, first_party_sets.db, ukm_db) and .greenhouse_session/ (351
# files, same file types) both got committed because neither matched any
# pattern below — this repo's rule is "if it contains personal data,
# credentials, or runtime state → exclude", and any Chrome profile directory
# always does, regardless of what it's named.
.*_session/
.*_session_*/
*_session_backup*/
data/session_backups/
# Chrome profile internals, in case a session dir is ever tracked from
# OUTSIDE one of the ignored directories above (e.g. copied/renamed) —
# belt and suspenders on top of the directory-level ignores. Note: gitignore
# patterns with spaces do NOT need quotes — a literal space in the pattern
# matches a literal space in the filename.
Cookies
Cookies-journal
Login Data
Login Data-journal
Login Data For Account
Login Data For Account-journal
Web Data
Web Data-journal
Account Web Data
Account Web Data-journal
History
Network Persistent State
Trust Tokens
Trust Tokens-journal
first_party_sets.db
first_party_sets.db-journal
ukm_db
*.pma
SingletonLock
SingletonCookie
SingletonSocket

# ── Generated output files (regenerated on each run) ─────────────────────────
resumes/
cover_letters/
output/
screenshots/
data/raw_jobs.csv
data/filtered_jobs.csv
data/linkedin_jobs.csv
data/indeed_jobs.csv
data/scheduler_*.log

# ── Personal documents accidentally committed ──────────────────────────────────
# resume files — contain real personal data
*.docx
# personal PDFs (LinkedIn carousel etc.)
*.pdf
*_jo.docx

# ── macOS metadata ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
data/.DS_Store

# ── Python cache ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python

# ── Claude / IDE metadata ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
*.test_persist.txt
test_persist.txt

# ── Dev scripts not meant for public use ─────────────────────────────────────
push_to_github.sh
_push.sh
